{{also|Appendix:Variations of "lob"}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lŏb}}, {{IPA|en|/lɒb/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lob.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒb|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
First attested late 16th c. in the sense "allow or cause to dangle, hang," from {{m|en|lob#Etymology_2|sense 2}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[throw]] or [[hit]] a [[ball]] into the [[air]] in a [[high]] [[arc]].
#: {{ux|en|The guard '''lobbed''' a pass just over the defender.}}
#: {{ux|en|The tennis player '''lobbed''' the ball, which was a costly mistake.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|colloquial}} To [[throw]].
#: {{syn|en|fling|hurl|Thesaurus:throw}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=Thailand: Anti-military party leader faces sedition charges| date=2019-04-06| accessdate=2019-04-06| author=Caleb Quinley| work=Al Jazeera| publisher=Al Jazeera| url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2019/04/thailand-anti-military-party-leader-faces-sedition-charges-190406052615231.html| location=Doha| passage=In the months leading up to the election, government representatives took up a cybercrime case against Thanathorn for criticising the government on a Facebook Live video... They also '''lobbed''' more legal cases at his party for allegedly spreading false information.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 December 29|author=Stephen Roberts|title=Stories and facts behind railway plaques: Chippenham (1841)|journal=RAIL|issue=947|page=57|text=I'm sure the Brunel-designed stone-built structure would have had a hatstand for his trademark stovepipe. I can picture him rocking up there of a morning and '''lobbing''' it nonchalantly onto the hatstand.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|colloquial}} To [[put]], [[place]].
#: {{syn|en|lay|lay down|put down|set down|deposit}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Lob''' the bacon in the pot.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|sports}} To [[hit]], [[kick]], or [[throw]] a ball over another player in a game.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=January 15, 2011|author=Nabil Hassan| title=Wigan 1 - 1 Fulham| work=BBC| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9358449.stm| passage=Wigan took the lead when Hugo Rodallega '''lobbed''' David Stockdale from close range having earlier headed against the post.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To let fall heavily or lazily.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 5|IV|ii|passage=And their poor jades / '''Lob''' down their heads.}}

